**(b) Both-week absolute values + changes** (source: ad platform, via check_performance / compare_windows)

| Metric | prior_week (10-17→10-23) | last_week (10-24→10-30) | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Spend | $3,761.84 | $3,039.99 | −$721.85 (−19.2%)* |
| Conversions | 19 | 16 | −3 (−15.8%)* |
| CPA | $197.99 | $190.00 | −$7.99 (−4.0%)* |

\* The comparison tool returns direction only ("down" for all three); the deltas above are simple arithmetic on the tool-returned totals, shown for sizing. Direction and both absolute totals are tool-reported.

**(c) Driver read — limitation up front:** My Meta tools return **account-level totals only**; no campaign or ad set rows are exposed. I cannot name any campaign or attribute the move to specific spend shifts or conversion drops at the campaign level — none were shown to me, and I will not invent them.

What the account-level pattern does show:
- Spend fell (−19.2%) faster than conversions (−15.8%), so CPA **improved** slightly (−$7.99, −4.0%). The WoW move is consistent with a broad spend reduction rather than a conversion-efficiency collapse: there was no CPA deterioration to explain.
- Both spend and conversions moved down together in the same direction, which fits a pacing/budget pullback; a delivery or tracking problem would typically show conversions falling while spend held.
- Per the analysis skill: a change I can see in totals but cannot attribute to a named driver is a **question to investigate** (e.g., pull campaign-level breakdown in Ads Manager), not a fact to report. I flag it as such rather than guessing.

**(d) Data completeness note**
- Both `check_performance` calls report `data_complete_through: 2026-10-30`, which equals the anchor date and the `last_week` window end. The last_week window is a full 7-day span ending at the anchor; nothing in the tool output indicates it is partial. Last complete date: **2026-10-30**.
- **Small-volume caveat:** 19 → 16 conversions is a 3-conversion difference. At this volume, weekly conversion counts are noisy and the −15.8% conversion change (and even the −4.0% CPA move) is within plausible week-to-week variation — do not over-read either.
- Source is the ad platform (fixture), per the platform context reminder; media metrics only — no warehouse/pipeline figures are mixed in here.

